From 81535e92f7afa9f43baee68812bc1ce88cef4949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: Exynos 9820 Mali-G76 support with CMU_G3D and
 G3D power domain

GPU of the Exynos 9820 (Galaxy S10/S10+):

 - clk: the CMU_G3D muxes, dividers and gates with their binding IDs.
   PLL_G3D and the G3D rail are owned by the ACPM firmware (DVFS_G3D);
   the CMU_G3D clocks are registered for visibility and for the
   suspend save/restore lists, no rate is propagated to the PLL.
 - pmdomain: the embedded G3D domain follows the vendor PMUCAL
   sequence. On: route PLL_G3D, cycle the outer G3D block, power the
   embedded G3D, restore the CMU_G3D and SYSREG_G3D registers lost by
   the outer block reset. Off: save them, power off, park the GPU mux
   on the oscillator and release the PLL. With samsung,dtzpc-addr the
   EL3 monitor saves the D_TZPC configuration of a domain before power
   off and restores it after power on, as the vendor kernel does;
   otherwise the SFRs can be left secure-only after a power cycle.
 - panfrost: compatible and platform data for the Mali-G76 MP12 with
   the setup the vendor kbase driver uses on this SoC: all 12 cores
   (the dead-core fuse is only logged), AARCH64_4K page tables with
   the kbase non-coherent values (GPU_COHERENCY_ENABLE = none,
   AS_MEMATTR 0x88 for cached mappings, no INA bits in AS_TRANSCFG).
   Job faults log the time since the last runtime resume.

The binding changes (pd-samsung, mali-bifrost) are part of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
